      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The argument for segregation as a \"preventative measure\" was framed around maintaining a rigid social hierarchy to prevent chaos. They would argue that mixing races inevitably led to social friction and that separate spheres of life were necessary to keep different groups orderly. They often claimed that the presence of other races introduced elements of instability or moral laxity into the established community structure. Essentially, they presented segregation not as oppression, but as a necessary form of social engineering to preserve the existing, supposedly superior, societal order.",
